Build and link dependencies
---------------------------

These are resolved by `find_package` at configure time; their source archives
are not committed to this repository. G46's developer-side source-bundle tool
accepts the locked official Eigen 3.4.0, fmt 9.1.0 and SUNDIALS 7.7.0 archives,
extracts the declared licence materials and gives both to the offline build.
Their packaging form and the files actually incorporated into or shipped with a
release still determine that release's final licence materials.

Eigen

    Licence   primarily MPL-2.0; individual files carry their own terms
    Form      header library; included Eigen code is compiled into ORVD objects

  Eigen is primarily MPL-2.0; some files carry BSD or additional LGPL terms.
  The configured Eigen distribution's `COPYING.README` and individual source
  files are authoritative. Upstream provides `EIGEN_MPL2_ONLY` to reject
  included LGPL code; the tracked ORVD target configuration does not define it.
  The subsequent release workflow must determine which Eigen files reach the
  release artifacts and carry the corresponding terms.

fmt

    Licence   MIT (Expat)
    Form      supplied through the configured `fmt::fmt` CMake target

  The configured package may provide fmt as a shared library, a static library,
  or another supported target form. A release that ships fmt material must carry
  the licence text belonging to that fmt version.

SUNDIALS 7.7.0

    Licence   BSD-3-Clause
    Form      CVODE, serial N_Vector, dense matrix and dense linear solver

  ORVD resolves these components through the configured SUNDIALS CMake package
  and links them into the first numerical backend. The G46 offline source bundle
  carries the locked upstream archive, LICENSE and NOTICE; a development build
  may instead provide the same package through a standard CMake search prefix.


